+# Patch 0029: in-app help, part 2 (B7b): the Help screen, plus three pages
+
+Items: B7b, and the 0029 pages from the B7 page plan. Status: `[x]` done and tested in my sandbox (pure logic, `tsc`, the whole suite), `[ ]` needs you (the screens are not run in my sandbox, so they are untested on a device).
+
+## What you asked for
+- Continue B7 in small chunks, three pages per patch. Cumulative depth confirmed (a chosen depth shows it plus the ones above it).
+
+## Steps
+1. [x] Checked the repo for updates (nothing newer than my 0028 commit).
+2. [x] `src/lib/mdBlocks.ts` (pure): the Markdown slice the pages use: headings, paragraphs, bullet and numbered lists (nested), tables with alignment, fenced code, mermaid blocks, and inline bold, italic, code and links. A link only becomes tappable if it is `(#/page-id)` or `http(s)://`; anything else (such as `javascript:`) is shown as text.
+3. [x] `src/lib/flowchart.ts` (pure): reads the Mermaid flowchart subset (`flowchart TD|LR`, `[box]`, `{decision}`, `(round)`, `-->`, `-->|label|`, chains, `;`, comments) and lays it out in layers: longest-path layers, branch ordering by neighbour position, loops handled (drawn dashed), nothing overlaps. Anything outside the subset returns null and the screen shows the source as text.
+4. [x] `src/ui/Markdown.tsx` and `src/ui/Flowchart.tsx` (react-native-svg, already a dependency): draw the above, follow the display mode's text size, scroll sideways when wide.
+5. [x] `src/lib/helpBuiltin.ts`: the copy of `help/help.json` that ships in the app, turned into pages and an index. Works with no internet.
+6. [x] `src/screens/Help.tsx`: search, a Basic / Deep / Advanced picker (remembered), a trail of parent pages, the page, "In this section", "Related" and "Pages that link here" lists, a Home button, and a back button that goes back through the pages you opened before leaving Help. Opens at a given page when the route has an `id` (for the "?" buttons in B7d).
+7. [x] More ▸ **Help** row (in every display mode, including Minimal and for every role), `help` route in `App.tsx`, `helpDepth` setting (default Basic, kept in backups).
+8. [x] Fixed by the new checks: a `;` inside a flowchart label was being treated as a statement break; the parser now respects brackets, and the page text avoids it anyway.
+9. [x] Pages: `sales/grid`, `sales/variants-and-stock`, `sales/scanners`. Each is Basic, Deep and Advanced. Every function and file named in them was checked against the code.
+10. [x] Tests: `tests/helpview.test.ts` (21: Markdown, flowchart parse and layout, every real flowchart is drawable and free of characters the website's Mermaid dislikes, every real page parses at every depth, the built-in bundle) and `tests/helpcitations.test.ts` (1: every file and function a page names in backticks exists; a mutation check confirmed it fails when a name is wrong). Suite: 327 pass, `tsc` clean.
+11. [x] `docs/PROGRESS.md`: patch log row, B7b and the 0029 pages ticked, N21 updated, new N27.
+12. [ ] You: N27, try the Help screen on the iPad and a phone.
+
+## Notes
+- The citations test means that renaming a function a page mentions will fail `npm test` until the page is updated. That is on purpose: the pages say they describe the app as it is.
+- Flowcharts scroll sideways if they are wider than the screen. A very wide diagram is drawn at full size rather than shrunk.
+- Not in this patch: fetching newer pages from a docs website (0030), "?" buttons on screens (B7d).
